From eb27f06afa55934ab600fd70fae133fbf2933a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:46:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] 0127: split the two kinds of coins into two HUD elements
 (6 total), drop the white bar

Coins, regional coins and moons are three separately adjustable groups now
(the player: the hexagon + 020 is a second kind of coins, the dots are the
moons). Regional coins is element 5 (appended: raw values 0-4 never change,
so saved settings survive); the state page grows to 18 floats and the
manual/hidden masks move to +0x248/+0x24C. The white bar under the counts
is gone from the editor (it has no matching pane in the game, a texture) --
not drawn, belongs to no group. All preview icons, the background, the
device frame, layout, fonts and colours are unchanged (0127 moves the
hexagon drawing verbatim, it does not redraw it). Compass/hints: not the
slot root cause (two panes each, within slots); their auto-edge and manual
paths are verified in the host test, and the hints pane name (TxtGuide01)
is still the unproven identification from 0123.
