+// hud_edge.c -- Super Mario Odyssey HUD edge anchor + launcher manual settings (0118 + 0119 + 0120 + 0123 + 0126 + 0127).
 //
 // The game's HUD (coins, moons, compass, lives, hints) is laid out for a 1280x720
 // (16:9) screen, so on a wider screen (iPhone 19.5:9) it sits inset from the
 // edges, and on a narrower screen (iPhone Duo 1.43:1, iPad 4:3) it would be
 // cut off at the edges. By default this hook pushes the HUD to the screen
 // edges, automatically adapting to the screen aspect (0118): the left widgets
-// (coins, moons) move left on a wider screen and right on a narrower one; the
+// (coins, regional coins, moons) move left on a wider screen and right on a narrower one; the
 // right widgets (compass, lives, hints) move right on a wider screen and left
 // on a narrower one. A manual setting made in the launcher's HUD editor (0119)
 // overrides the automatic edge anchor for that element: it is moved, resized
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@
